JIT: keep the unaligned flag of a struct that is returned in a register (applies after perf-35).

LowerRetStruct turns the GT_BLK of a returned struct into a GT_IND with ChangeOper, which keeps only
the common flags. The load of Unsafe.ReadUnaligned<T> lost GTF_IND_UNALIGNED that way, and a target
without unaligned access (JitNoUnalignedAccess) loaded it whole. The flag is carried over, as
TryTransformStoreObjAsStoreInd does for a store.

Regression test: bflat-ts:alignment/unaligned_access
Regression test: bflat-ts:alignment/unaligned_access_byte_wise

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/lower.cpp
@@ -6078,7 +6078,11 @@ void Lowering::LowerRetStruct(GenTreeUnOp* ret)
                 break;
             }
 
+            // ChangeOper keeps only the common flags, and an unaligned block load must stay unaligned: a target
+            // without unaligned access (JitNoUnalignedAccess) expands the scalar load.
+            const GenTreeFlags unaligned = retVal->gtFlags & GTF_IND_UNALIGNED;
             retVal->ChangeOper(GT_IND);
+            retVal->gtFlags |= unaligned;
             retVal->ChangeType(nativeReturnType);
             LowerIndir(retVal->AsIndir());
             break;
